<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="description" content="Connect your AI assistant to AgendaClock so it can build and update your meeting timelines for you.">
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
    <meta name="author" content="Greg Vanoni">

    <title>Connect your AI assistant - AgendaClock</title>
    <% include meeting_header %>
  </head>
  <body class="bg-light">

<div class="container">
  <main>
    <div class="py-5 text-center">
      <h2>Connect your AI assistant</h2>
      <p class="lead">Describe your meeting in plain words and let your AI assistant (Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor and others) build the timeline for you. No typing agenda rows by hand.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card mb-4">
      <div class="card-body">
        <div class="row">
          <div class="col-md-6">
            <h5>What is this?</h5>
            <p>Normally your AI assistant can't see or change anything in AgendaClock. A <strong>token</strong> is a temporary password you hand to your assistant so it can work on your timelines for you. The connection it uses is called <strong>MCP</strong>, a standard way for AI tools to plug into apps. You don't need to understand it: you only paste two things into your AI tool.</p>
            <h5>Why would I want it?</h5>
            <ul class="mb-md-0">
              <li>Turn a pasted agenda, email or doc into a timed timeline in seconds</li>
              <li>Change things by asking, instead of clicking through the editor</li>
              <li>Reuse last week's meeting as a starting point</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="col-md-6">
            <h5>Things you can say once connected</h5>
            <ul>
              <li>"Make a 45-minute team standup for 9:00 AM Phoenix time: 5 min intros, 30 min updates, 10 min wrap-up."</li>
              <li>"Here's my agenda from this email. Turn it into an AgendaClock timeline and give me the link."</li>
              <li>"Move Thursday's kickoff to 2:30 PM and give the demo 10 more minutes."</li>
              <li>"Show my timelines."</li>
            </ul>
            <h5>How to connect (about 2 minutes)</h5>
            <ol class="mb-0">
              <li><strong>Create a token</strong> below and copy it.</li>
              <li><strong>Click "Copy everything for my agent"</strong> and paste it to your AI agent (Muse, Claude and others). It sets itself up.</li>
              <li><strong>Ask for what you want.</strong> Prefer doing it by hand? The address is <code><%= endpoint %></code>.</li>
            </ol>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <% if (error) { %>
      <div class="alert alert-danger" role="alert"><%= error %></div>
    <% } %>

    <% if (newToken) { %>
      <div class="alert alert-success" role="alert">
        <h4 class="alert-heading">Your token is ready - copy it now</h4>
        <p>This is the only time the token is shown. It is not stored anywhere you can see again.</p>
        <p><code id="new-token-secret" style="word-break: break-all;"><%= newToken.secret %></code></p>
        <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-success" type="button" id="copy-token-btn">Copy token</button>
        <p class="mb-0 mt-2"><small>Token "<%= newToken.name %>" expires on <%= new Date(newToken.expiresAt).toLocaleString() %> (<%= newToken.ttlDays %> days). </small></p>
        <hr>
        <h5>Easiest: hand it to your AI agent (Muse and others)</h5>
        <p class="mb-2">Copy this whole message and paste it to your agent. It has everything the agent needs to connect by itself.</p>
        <pre id="agent-setup" class="bg-white border rounded p-2" style="white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-word;">Please connect to my AgendaClock account so you can create and edit my meeting timelines.

AgendaClock has an MCP server (Streamable HTTP). Add it as an MCP server / connector with:
- Name: agendaclock
- URL: <%= endpoint %>
- HTTP header: Authorization: Bearer <%= newToken.secret %>

If you set up MCP servers with a command, run:
claude mcp add --transport http agendaclock <%= endpoint %> --header "Authorization: Bearer <%= newToken.secret %>"

If you use a JSON settings file, add:
{"mcpServers":{"agendaclock":{"url":"<%= endpoint %>","headers":{"Authorization":"Bearer <%= newToken.secret %>"}}}}

Tools available: list_timelines, get_timeline, create_timeline, update_timeline (no delete).
This token is a secret: store it only in your MCP settings and do not repeat it back to me. It expires on <%= new Date(newToken.expiresAt).toDateString() %>.
When connected, call list_timelines and tell me what you find.</pre>
        <button class="btn btn-success mb-3" type="button" data-copy="agent-setup">Copy everything for my agent</button>

        <details class="mb-2">
          <summary>Claude Code: one command for your terminal</summary>
          <pre id="cmd-claude" class="bg-white border rounded p-2 mt-2" style="white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-all;">claude mcp add --transport http agendaclock <%= endpoint %> --header "Authorization: Bearer <%= newToken.secret %>"</pre>
          <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-success" type="button" data-copy="cmd-claude">Copy command</button>
        </details>
        <details class="mb-2">
          <summary>Cursor and other tools that use a settings file</summary>
          <pre id="cmd-json" class="bg-white border rounded p-2 mt-2" style="white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-all;">{
  "mcpServers": {
    "agendaclock": {
      "url": "<%= endpoint %>",
      "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer <%= newToken.secret %>" }
    }
  }
}</pre>
          <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-success" type="button" data-copy="cmd-json">Copy settings</button>
        </details>
        <p class="mb-0"><small>Setting it up by hand? The address is <code><%= endpoint %></code>, the header name is <code>Authorization</code> and the value is <code>Bearer</code>, a space, then your token.</small></p>
      </div>
    <% } %>

    <div class="row g-3">
      <div class="col-md-5 col-lg-4 order-md-last">
        <h4 class="mb-3">What your assistant can do</h4>
        <ul class="list-group mb-3">
          <li class="list-group-item">See the list of your timelines</li>
          <li class="list-group-item">Read one of your timelines</li>
          <li class="list-group-item">Create a new timeline for you</li>
          <li class="list-group-item">Change a timeline you own (title, time, agenda, look)</li>
          <li class="list-group-item text-muted">It can never delete a timeline</li>
        </ul>
        <h5>Is it safe?</h5>
        <p class="text-muted"><small>A token only works on your own timelines (<%= user.email %>). It can't see your Google account, email or anyone else's meetings. It stops working by itself when it expires, and you can switch it off any time with Revoke. Treat it like a password: only paste it into AI tools you trust.</small></p>
        <p><a href="/meeting/">Back to your timelines</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="col-md-7 col-lg-8">
        <h4 class="mb-3">Create a token</h4>
        <form method="POST" action="/mcp/tokens" class="mb-4">
          <div class="form-group">
            <label for="token-name">Name</label>
            <input type="text" class="form-control" id="token-name" name="name" maxlength="80" placeholder="e.g. Claude on my laptop" required>
            <small class="form-text text-muted">A label for you, so you remember which AI tool uses this token.</small>
          </div>
          <div class="form-group">
            <label>How long should it work?</label>
            <div>
              <% allowedTtlDays.forEach(function(days) { %>
                <div class="form-check form-check-inline">
                  <input class="form-check-input" type="radio" name="ttl_days" id="ttl-<%= days %>" value="<%= days %>" <%= days === 30 ? 'checked' : '' %>>
                  <label class="form-check-label" for="ttl-<%= days %>"><%= days %> days</label>
                </div>
              <% }); %>
            </div>
            <small class="form-text text-muted">After this it switches itself off. Come back here and create a new one whenever you need it.</small>
          </div>
          <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Create token</button>
        </form>

        <h4 class="mb-3">Your tokens</h4>
        <% if (tokens.length === 0) { %>
          <p class="text-muted">No tokens yet. Create one above.</p>
        <% } else { %>
          <table class="table table-sm">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Name</th>
                <th>Created</th>
                <th>Expires</th>
                <th>Last used</th>
                <th></th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <% tokens.forEach(function(t) { %>
                <tr>
                  <td><%= t.name %><br><small class="text-muted"><%= t.id %></small></td>
                  <td><%= t.createdAt ? new Date(t.createdAt).toLocaleDateString() : '-' %></td>
                  <td><%= t.expiresAt ? new Date(t.expiresAt).toLocaleDateString() : '-' %></td>
                  <td><%= t.lastUsedAt ? new Date(t.lastUsedAt).toLocaleString() : 'Never' %></td>
                  <td>
                    <form method="POST" action="/mcp/tokens/<%= t.id %>/revoke" onsubmit="return confirm('Revoke this token? Any AI tool using it stops working immediately.');">
                      <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-danger" type="submit">Revoke</button>
                    </form>
                  </td>
                </tr>
              <% }); %>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        <% } %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</div>

  <% include meeting_footer %>
  <script>
    document.addEventListener('click', function(e) {
      var btn = e.target;
      if (!btn) return;
      var targetId = btn.id === 'copy-token-btn' ? 'new-token-secret' : btn.getAttribute && btn.getAttribute('data-copy');
      if (!targetId) return;
      var label = btn.textContent;
      navigator.clipboard.writeText(document.getElementById(targetId).textContent.trim()).then(function() {
        btn.textContent = 'Copied!';
        setTimeout(function() { btn.textContent = label; }, 2000);
      });
    });
  </script>

  </body>
</html>
